Classic screen bitmap layout regression
======================================

Build test-intuition-screenbitmap or test-intuition-screenbitmap-quick.
The native Amiga Intuition component selects normal and quick targets.
Run on an AGA machine with at least 2 MiB Chip RAM.

Open eight-plane screens with caller-owned separate and interleaved planes.
Check the drawing/display headers, original header preservation, and a
physical pixel write on a later row. ChangeScreenBuffer must also preserve
the complete layout when refreshing Screen.BitMap_OBSOLETE. In particular,
an interleaved bitmap advances by 320 bytes per row, not the 40 bytes derived
from its 320-pixel width.

Preloaded pixels must also survive opening a screen with LAYERS_NOBACKFILL
or a custom no-op SA_BackFill hook, as used by PicBoot. The normal default
background clearing path is exercised separately.
